Bootstrap: docker
From: debian:bookworm-slim

%post
    set -eu
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    apt-get update
    apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
        ca-certificates curl git jq \
        nodejs npm \
        python3 python3-pip python3-venv
    apt-get clean
    rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

%help
    Sandbox for running one OpenCode benchmark case in isolation.
    opencode and yul binaries are bind-mounted in at run time (see
    benchmark/run_case_opencode_deepseek.sh), not baked into the image,
    so the harness always uses whatever's currently built/installed on
    the host without rebuilding the image.

    Docker equivalent (for hosts without Apptainer): see
    benchmark/Dockerfile.opencode-sandbox - keep both package lists in
    sync. run_case_opencode_deepseek.sh auto-detects which runtime is on
    PATH (or set CONTAINER_RUNTIME=apptainer|docker to force one).
